<section class="pkg-faq-band">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="pkg-faq">
      <details><summary>How do I help my elderly parent move home?</summary><p>Start with a calm conversation about what they want, then agree a timeline. A coordinator can then manage sorting, packing, the removal and settling in. Chayce offers a Discovery Consultation from &pound;150 to create the plan with your family.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you manage the move if I live far away?</summary><p>Yes. Your dedicated coordinator handles the work on the ground and keeps you updated by phone or email, so you do not need to be there for every step.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you help with moves into retirement villages?</summary><p>Yes. We plan and carry out moves into retirement villages and smaller homes anywhere in the UK, including help downsizing to fit the new space.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How much does it cost to move an elderly parent in the UK?</summary><p>Packages start at &pound;995 for packing and removals and &pound;1,850 for a full-service move. The right one depends on the size of the home and how much support is needed.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is my parent's move insured?</summary><p>Yes. Every removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

